comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T22:29:01.605Z",codex-root,"Duplicate search across all 61 items found no canonical Monica main/Sanctum users/vaults edition item. Stable 4.x parity and source freshness remain closed predecessors, so this is a new child of monica-platform rather than a reopened duplicate."
  "2026-07-25T22:57:06.623Z",codex-root,"Latest-source research verified stable 4.x at v4.1.2 and current main at its public head. The current route inventory contains GET /user, GET /users, GET /users/{user}, and six vault CRUD routes; CLI source-status keeps stable and next provenance separate so current main does not silently redefine the stable contract."
  "2026-07-25T22:57:12.074Z",codex-root,"Privacy-safe live acceptance completed with the actual monica executable: 108 checks, 52 passes, 56 expected infrastructure-unavailable outcomes, and 0 unexpected failures. Stable/next source checks and schemas pass; POST, PUT, PATCH, and DELETE vault commands were each blocked before network access. Settings were restored and no live payloads were persisted in the repository."
  "2026-07-25T23:01:31.801Z",codex-root,"Full release gate passed: 865 tests at exact 100/100/100/100, 611/611 documented exports, every source file at or below 300 code lines, 4.27 percent duplicated lines below the 5 percent gate, 285/285 help checks, clean Bun dependency/history/version audits, and isolated npx plus bunx package consumers reporting 2026.7.25."
  "2026-07-25T23:16:03.295Z",codex-root,Final artifact review added an explicit no-op PATCH rejection so vaults patch cannot send an empty payload; focused tests and full 100/100/100/100 coverage pass afterward. The bundled next source commit was rechecked against the public main head and remains current.
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T22:29:01.605Z",codex-root,"Authoritative sources: monicahq/monica main routes/api.php and its UserController, VaultController, UserResource, and VaultResource. Private settings and payloads remain outside the repository under ~/.monica-cli."
  "2026-07-25T22:57:08.626Z",codex-root,"Connection verification falls back from stable /me to current /user only on HTTP 404 or 405. Authentication, timeout, and infrastructure errors are preserved without fallback so diagnostics cannot misclassify a broken server as an edition mismatch."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T22:29:01.605Z",codex-root,"API completeness must be edition-specific: stable 4.x and current main expose disjoint route sets and authentication stacks, so a single unversioned parity percentage is misleading."
  "2026-07-25T22:57:10.617Z",codex-root,"The live instance still fails authenticated bootstrap while fetching Cloudflare trust-proxy ranges. Treat that as infrastructure unavailable, not endpoint unsupported; public provenance and local schema checks remain valid, while only a successful or route-specific response can establish compatibility."
