close_reason: Implemented and verified every current Monica main API route while preserving the complete stable 4.x edition.
body: "## Context\nMonica stable 4.x remains fully mapped, but authoritative main now exposes a separate Sanctum API for the authenticated user, account users, and vault CRUD. The CLI currently models only stable 4.x, so agents cannot reason about or invoke the latest available API edition.\n\n## Delivery\n- Preserve the stable 4.x catalog while adding an authoritative main-edition catalog and freshness verification.\n- Add typed users and vaults command groups for every current main API route.\n- Detect and document edition compatibility without misclassifying unavailable infrastructure.\n- Keep default TOON, JSON/YAML/Markdown/table schemas, agent exports, setup/doctor guidance, and help contracts aligned.\n- Upgrade repository PM tooling to the latest compatible published versions.\n\n## Safety\nLive acceptance is GET-only with readOnlyMode enabled. Mutations are covered by mocked integration tests and must be rejected before network access against the private instance. No credentials, user/vault identifiers, response payloads, or signed paths may enter Git, PM, logs, or GitHub."
